# Ship after change

When you finish work that should run on this product’s **local or production** host (API, `dist` SPA, Worker assets, schema used by prod), **publish using that product’s deploy map** before ending the turn—unless the user explicitly says not to deploy.

**Keep local and prod in sync.** Git commit/push alone is not enough when the user asked to ship or the work is meant to be live. When the user asks to **commit and push** (or SPCD / ship) for shippable app changes, **also deploy** per the product map in the same turn unless they say otherwise.

## Deploy map

Commands live in ALGR [`sites.json`](../../sites.json) under each product’s `deploy` array. Full playbook: `docs/prompts/ship-after-change.md`.

## Do not

- Assume remote/tunnel will magically pick up an unbuilt `dist/`
- Skip migrations when Prisma schema changed
- Batch unrelated products’ deploys
- Leave prod on an older build after pushing shippable changes the user expected live
